.nh
.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Aug 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-service-expose - Expose a local service on the AceTeam Network gateway


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel service expose  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Serves a local port on this node's gateway at /expose//, gated by a
visibility level.

.PP
private  only the creator (requires a caller identity the backend supplies,
           so a local CLI cannot grant it — use org or link)
  org      any member of your organization on the network
  link     anyone holding the signed, expiring link token

.PP
Requires the node gateway to be running (citadel work).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for expose

.PP
\fB--port\fP=0
	Local port the service listens on (required)

.PP
\fB--ttl\fP=24h0m0s
	Lifetime of a --visibility link token

.PP
\fB--visibility\fP="org"
	Who may reach it: org or link


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Expose the nvr module's Frigate UI to your organization
  citadel service expose frigate --port 8212 --visibility org

  # Share a dashboard by link for 2 hours
  citadel service expose grafana --port 3000 --visibility link --ttl 2h
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel-service(1)\fP
